From 8233faaf8c94dfabfc13451687a15d69b93a91a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:22:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(truth): one domain, one company, one price list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0022. The site was two businesses wearing one skin, and both were live.

TWO PRICE LISTS ON ONE PAGE

/pricing rendered Power Audit EUR 25k-45k and Feasibility Study EUR 45k-95k above
the real engagement ladder starting at EUR 4,500. Neither upper band existed
anywhere in gridforge/commercial.py, so the parity test could not see them and
nothing failed. PACKAGES is gone; the catalogue is the only price list.

MEGAWATTS WE DO NOT HAVE

/infrastructure was a whole page selling containerised behind-the-meter power
blocks by the megawatt — gensets, BESS, footprints, weeks-to-energised, "stand up a
megawatt while the queue says 2031". The homepage carried the same offer three more
times: reference architectures to 120 MW+, a configurator sizing campus builds, and
a single-line diagram of a facility we would design.

We do not build, own, finance or operate any of it, and the capital rule puts it
out of scope permanently. Sizing envelopes for plant we would never supply are
fictitious capacity wearing the clothes of a product sheet. Page, sections,
components and catalogue removed.

THE ASSISTANT WAS THE WORST OF IT

/api/chat's system prompt was a confident, detailed briefing for the company that
no longer exists: REF-01 hybrid microgrids, a 400-800 V DC bus, an EMS doing
FCR/aFRR, and that same phantom fee list. A page can be skimmed; an assistant
answers the specific question a buyer actually asked, in a tone that sounds like it
knows. Its engagement list is now generated from lib/products.ts and it is told
plainly what to refuse.

ONE DOMAIN

Six files hardcoded gridforge-ai.vercel.app — layout metadata, JSON-LD, robots,
sitemap, llms.txt and the citation endpoint — while seven hardcoded timetopower.ai
for emails, Stripe URLs and deliverable links.

Every canonical URL, every sitemap entry and the citation we ASK PEOPLE TO USE
pointed at a preview domain. That splits search authority away from the domain that
serves the site, and the whole reference and agent-distribution layer built in 0017
and 0018 was advertising the wrong home. SITE_URL in lib/site.ts is now the only
definition, overridable with NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL for previews.

THE BAND THAT COULD NOT BE CHECKED

"Deposit against EUR 22k-45k" had the 22 in the engine and the 45 typed into a React
component, so half of every quoted range was unsourceable. Engagement.price_eur_max
carries the top of the band, opensBandCents mirrors it, the ladder renders from it,
and the parity test asserts the two agree.

TESTS

11 new (377 total). No file hardcodes a site URL outside the registry. No euro
figure exists outside the catalogue — that test is what found the EUR 25k-45k still
sitting in the chat prompt after I thought I had finished. SERVICES may not offer a
microgrid, HVDC distribution, an EMS or a Power Audit. No file offers POWER_BLOCKS,
CONFIG_VARIANTS or "megawatts in months", with comments stripped first so the
history of why they went can stay in the file. MARKET_STATS must survive with its
sources: removing our own invented capacity is not a reason to remove sourced
figures about the market the buyer lives in.

Set NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://timetopower.ai on Vercel.

tsc clean, lint clean, build clean, reference artefacts unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
